FUN_00430d0e: split-off object-block loader shares its CALLERS' stack frame

FUN_00430d0e @0x430d0e is not a real function: it is the tail fragment of
Init_Scene_Objects/Init_Track_Objects (Ghidra split it because both jump into it).
It addresses the CALLER's frame through the dropped EBP (unaff_EBP-0x48 = the
14-entry active-block array local_4c/aiStack_4c, unaff_EBP-0x10 = the current
strip-object pointer local iVar3/iStack_14) and receives ESI (search index) and
EBX (block number) live from the caller. The _g_ebp static default made every
frame access a wild pointer (L1-7 crash after the jumptable fix).
Reconstruct with explicit parameters (blocks[], cur, esi, ebx): frame offsets
-0x48/-0x44+i map to blocks[0]/byte-offset reads, -0x10 becomes the local _curv
(the fragment itself rewrites it per iteration), the self-recursion (Ghidra's
rendering of the jump back to the fragment head) passes the current state, and
both call sites pass their locals (esi==0xe and ebx==-1 are compile-time facts
at those sites: the calls sit inside `if (search==0xe)` / `if (block==-1)`).

